Changelog: 28-11-2026 15:54:35

Fixed. The run wrapper points shellcheck at core's gamelog.sh from the repository's root, so the shell check in CI reads it.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 15:48:05

Added. When the window opens without a controller, a desktop notification says so and asks to switch it on or press its PS button (owner, 28-11-2026). The app's log notes it as a warning.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 15:36:57

Added. The emulator log says what each game ran with and how it ended, through core's gamelog.sh (owner, 28-11-2026). Every line has the time and a level, also what shadPS4 prints. Before the game it names the build, the board, the processor, the game, each controller, the displays and the desktop's mode. After the game it gives the exit code with its signal, the time the game ran and the system log's crashes. A crash is an ERROR.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 13:22:41

Release 1.9.2.

Changelog: 28-11-2026 12:38:25

Fixed. The app is called PS5 shadPS4 Manager now, with the device's name in front (owner, 28-11-2026). The window, the menu entry, the run script's messages and the wiki use that name. The Steam collection keeps the tag shadPS4 Manager, so the shortcuts already in Steam stay in one collection.

Changelog: 27-11-2026 19:59:41

Release 1.9.1.

Changelog: 26-11-2026 14:03:51

Release 1.9.0.

Changelog: 26-11-2026 12:21:07

Added. What shadPS4 prints while a game runs now goes to the app's emulator log, emulator.log beside the app's own
log. Before, ps5-shadps4-run started shadPS4 in its place, so the output went to Steam's console only. The run
wrapper now stays while shadPS4 runs. It writes a started and an ended line around each run, with shadPS4's exit
code. Every line shows the home folder as ~. The file turns over at 1 MB with three older ones kept. The wrapper
passes a stop from Steam on to shadPS4 and ends with shadPS4's exit code. Two radio buttons at the top of the View
logs tab choose the app's log or shadPS4's. Clear logs empties the log shown.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 17:44:44

Release 1.8.1.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 21:58:22

Release 1.8.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 21:22:28

Added. Exit shadPS4 is the first button under the games table. It ends shadPS4 at once, with everything it started, and
asks nothing first. It is on only while shadPS4 runs. A game that runs ends without saving, as its tooltip says. The
line under the tabs then says "shadPS4 was ended." The app finds shadPS4's processes with core's new processes module.
The wiki chapter has a new section, Exit shadPS4.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 20:00:16

Release 1.7.1.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 18:07:36

Fixed. tests/test_main_window.py.orig, an old copy of a test file that nothing used, is gone.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 15:55:10

Fixed. The app's files that had no license line have one now, the arrow of its lists among them.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 15:19:54

Fixed. The states beside the title now use two colors: green when all is well, red when not. A warning and an off state,
such as Not installed or shadNet Off, are red now. The wiki says so.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 12:25:09

Release 1.7.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 11:44:56

Added. The row beside the title has a new state, Steam. Its dot is green while Steam runs and is signed in, and red when
it is not, because a game in Steam starts only then. The app looks again every few seconds. The states now show their
names alone, Installed, shadNet, Controller and Steam, and the dot's color shows the state. Each tooltip opens with the
state in full, such as Not installed or No controller. The wiki describes the row. test_main_window.py tests the Steam
state and follows the new order.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 12:04:44

Release 1.6.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 19:26:09

Release 1.5.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 18:49:34

Added. The window's new order (owner, 20-11-2026). The header's pills are the shadPS4 version, shadPS4 Install,
shadPS4 Uninstall and Refresh. The row under them is Games Install, Games Uninstall, Available in Steam, shadNet
Account and Play time. Games Uninstall is new: it is what the Remove game… button under the table did, and that
button went. The Your games box went. Under the pills are two columns: the four state lines, each name with a colon
(shadPS4:, Sys modules:, Game folders:, shadNet:), and beside them Installed version:, the shadPS4 version in use.
The tabs are Your games, Start game, Memory cards, Settings, View logs (it was Log) and Clear logs.

Added. A check for a game that is in Steam more than once (owner, 20-11-2026). The app says which games and how
often, the game's In Steam box says it in its tooltip, and Update Steam lights and leaves one shortcut of each, with
the latest play time; its question says how many double shortcuts go.

Fixed. The chosen row of a table is 30 % blue, with the theme's text color: filled with the header's blue, a chosen
first row could hardly be told from the header above it.

Fixed. Start game with Steam closed started Steam and never the game, while the line said "Steam starts". The app
now starts Steam first, waits until it takes commands, then gives it the game's address, again when the game does
not come up (core's play). The line says the game runs only once shadPS4 does, and says when Steam did not start it.
While shadPS4 runs already, Start game starts no second one.

Fixed. A shortcut whose fields Steam wrote in lower case (exe, launchoptions) was not recognized as the app's, so
Update Steam added the game a second time. They are read whatever their case now.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 13:11:18

Release 1.4.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 03:39:29

Added. The version manager (owner, 20-11-2026: as shadPS4's own launcher has one; core's builds). The version box in
the header is a pill: its menu lists the shadPS4 builds installed and puts another in use, and Manage versions… opens
the version manager, which downloads the stable releases and the pre-release (a nightly) from GitHub, checked against
the SHA-256 GitHub publishes, adds a custom AppImage, puts a build in use and deletes one. Builds stay side by side:
Install no longer deletes the others, and puts the build this version was tried with back in use, without a download
when it is still there. Uninstall removes every build. A build other than the tested one is said to be not tried on
the board.

Changelog: 19-11-2026 22:33:16

Release 1.3.1.

Changelog: 19-11-2026 22:12:37

Fixed. The message about a newer build says it comes once it has been tried on the board, not the console (owner, 19-11-2026: board everywhere).

Changelog: 18-11-2026 04:15:16

Release 1.3.0.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 02:50:27

Added. The managers' new design, as PPSSPP Manager's, PCSX2 Manager's and RPCS3 Manager's: a Memory cards tab
with the saves shadPS4 keeps, each under its game's title (export to a .zip, import, delete). Clear logs, a tab
beside Log that is a button, empties the app's log file and the Log tab and removes the older log files. Start
game stands beside Your games. The six tabs share the window's whole width and are pills as the ones above them.
Play time moved from the header to the row of action pills. Under the header's pills only the links to shadPS4's
release notes and the wiki are left, in the type of a pill's caption; the introduction went. shadPS4's state is
one line. Under the games an info symbol stands in for the line of text about Steam. The window opens 900 wide
(it was 980), which is its narrowest, and 606 high (it was 800); the Settings tab scrolls when it is higher than
the window.

